house of the dragon is full of new faces  and not all of them used to belong to  the doctor here's where else you've seen  the talented cast  someone must always sit on the iron  throne and at the start of house of the  dragon that responsibility falls to king  viserys targaryen played by veteran  actor patty considine king viserys is  described in hbo's official promotions  for the series as a good man setting him  miles apart from the game of thrones  character who later bears his name  outside of westeros considine has had a  long and varied career in both film and  television a versatile and lauded  performer he's equally well known for  indie films like dead man's shoes and in  america and big budget blockbusters like  the born ultimatum  i can't think  we can't laugh i can't cry  i can't  he's also collaborated with simon pegg  and nick frost on hot fuzz and the  world's end considine's other major tv  roles include claude bolton in the  stephen king adaptation the outsider and  the despicable father john hughes in the  british crime saga peaky blinders  though the targaryens are at the center  of house of the dragon they're far from  the only great house in westeros with a  stake in the game one of the other major  players is house hightower a family that  doesn't play an especially major role in  game of thrones but which has a long and  storied history on the continent one of  the main characters in house of the  dragon is alison hightower daughter of  sir otto hightower the hand of the king  teenage allison is played by newcomer  emily carey alison hightower is brought  to life as an adult by english actor  olivia cook a young star who's  nonetheless accrued a lot of notable  credits in her career  reuben you hurt yourself  you hurt me  i'll hurt myself too i'll hurt myself  too  cook first rose to prominence starring  in a couple of bbc miniseries including  the secret of prickly hall alongside  game of thrones star maisie williams  she's also applied her trade in the  alfred hitchcock inspired series bates  motel and the itv historical drama  vanity fair on the big screen cook has  appeared in films like sound of metal  and steven spielberg's ready player one  what would a song of ice and fire be  without a few cool enigmatic rogue  warrior types that's the archetype that  lord corliss velardian falls into in  house of the dragon though you'd be  wrong to write him off as simply a trope  viewed in his day as the best sea  captain in all of westeros cordless  hails from a family nearly as  prestigious as house targaryen a key  part of the royal court and a respected  ruler in his own right the sea snake  isn't a man to be trifled with  four ships have now been lost the last  one was flying my banner you might not  immediately recognize the name steve  toussaint but you've almost certainly  seen him in something the hollywood  veteran has had a long career with  credits that range from genre affair  like prince of persia the sands of time  to serious dramas on the stage and  screen toussaint is most prolific on  television though with roles in the noc  inspector lewis and netflix's pine gap  at the center of the drama in house of  the dragon is prince daemon targaryen  played by british star matt smith the  younger brother of king viserys and  uncle to princess rhaenyra damon is a  dragon rider warrior and all-around  major player in the politics of  continent a complicated figure to say  the least he played a major role in the  dance of the dragons and the preceding  political turmoil in part because of his  own desire for power most fans of sci-fi  and fantasy television will instantly  recognize smith as the 11th doctor in  doctor who a role he played for three  seasons from 2010 to 2013 and for which  he gained widespread acclaim a very  skinny  that is proper skinny i've never seen it  from the outside fans of historical  dramas may know smith better for his  role as prince philip in netflix's the  crown a performance that earned him a  primetime emmy nomination in 2018. on  the big screen smith is known for roles  like jack in edgar wright's last night  in soho alex and terminator genesis and  the villainous milo in morbius  the main action of house of the dragon  proceeds and involves the dance of the  dragons a civil war of sorts fought  between different targaryen claimants to  the iron throne one of those claimants  is princess rhaenyra targaryen played as  an adult by emma darcy an actor equally  at home on the stage and the screen  darcy started out in various live  theater productions in the uk before  landing some tv and film roles darcy  appeared in the 2020 british comedy  misbehavior the bbc drama baptist and  the itv comedy drama wild bill just to  name a few roles the role of rhaenyra in  house of the dragon is undoubtedly  darcy's highest profile role to date one  shared by australian newcomer millie  alcock who plays the princess as a 15  year old  every game of thrones fan knows what an  important and often dangerous position  the hand of the king is in westeros  depending on the current monarch of the  land the hand may wind up being the true  ruler behind the scenes like his father  before him king viserys targaryen relies  on otto hightower as his hand played in  house of the dragon by rhys evans a  long-standing member of the royal court  and a man of nearly impeccable  reputation otto is also the father of  allison hightower a role that ends up  pulling him even further into the messy  family politics of the targaryens a  welsh actor and longtime star of the  screen evans is probably best known for  his roles in notting hill come on open  up  this is me  spikey the harry potter franchise and as  dr kurt connors aka the lizard in the  amazing spider-man evens has also had a  number of prominent television roles  including playing sherlock holmes older  brother mycroft in the cbs crime  procedural elementary  dragon rider overlooked air and wife to  the sea snake cordless velaryon princess  rhaenys targaryen occupies a unique role  in the royal court of westeros rhaenys  carries the less than proud nickname of  the queen who never was a reference to  her being passed up as successor to king  joharis targaryen the first in favor of  her cousin paserus being denied the iron  throne does little to curb princess  rhaenys's influence and drive however  and she forms a fearsome couple with her  seafaring husband raynese is played by  tv stalwart eve best in house of the  dragon best is probably most  recognizable for her long-standing role  as dr eleanor o'hara in nurse jackie and  for her supporting performance as  wallace simpson in the king's speech  more recently she appeared in the bbc  miniseries the honorable woman and  netflix's teen fantasy show fate the  wink saga  initially an outsider in the court of  king viserys targaryen rosaria isn't  even a native of westeros and yet she  eventually rises to become what hbo  calls the most trusted and most unlikely  ally of prince damon targaryen visaria  is brought to life by sonoya mizuno an  actor arguably known best for her many  collaborations with sci-fi autur alex  garland mizuno has featured in several  of garland's projects including ex  machina and the cosmic horror  masterpiece annihilation her other film  credits include crazy rich asians beauty  and the beast and la la land  neither a lord nor a ruler sir kristen  cole might seem at first like the odd  man out in the main cast of house of the  dragon being common born he's not  exactly overflowing with riches or power  but he manages to defeat daemon  targaryen in combat in the premiere  episode and make a strong impression on  princess rhaenyra just as kristin cole  is a bit of an unknown quantity in house  of the dragon so too is the actor fabian  frankel the least established star in  the main cast a graduate of the royal  academy of dramatic art and the london  academy of music and dramatic art  frankel got his big break in the bbc one  mini-series the serpent which tells the  terrifying real-life story of a french  serial killer he also appeared in the  2019 romantic comedy last christmas  alongside game of thrones star emilia  clark  where would a king of westeros be  without his kingsguard the white-cloaked  guardians of the royal family have  always played a key role in a song of  ice and fire and that tradition  continues in house of the dragon as lord  commander of the kingsguard during the  reign of king viserys targaryen sir  harold westerling has a lot on his plate  house of the dragon sets him in a  tumultuous time for the family he's  sworn to protect but he carries himself  with dignity and professionalism  nonetheless fans of the fantasy genre  should be well acquainted with grier  mctavish the actor responsible for  embodying sir harold in house of the  dragon he appears in all three of peter  jackson's the hobbit films as well as  the star's time travel fantasy epic  outlander  it's fiction  outlandish fiction just as comfortable  in a voice booth mctavish has lent his  vocal talents to a number of video games  and animated series and films including  dracula in netflix's critically  acclaimed castlevania series that all  barely even scratches the surface of  mctavish's career which also includes  credits like the saint of killers and  preacher among many other smaller roles  while the family may not be too  important during the events of game of  thrones one particular member of house  beesbury lord lyman plays a key role in  house of the dragon as an ally of the  high towers and the master of coin on  king viserys small council this  otherwise unassuming man holds a  substantial amount of influence in the  realm at the start of the show who  better to portray an unassuming belord  than experienced character actor bill  patterson the scott is best known in  recent times for playing phoebe  wallerbridge's father in fleabag of  every star on this list patterson may  have the longest resume as his on-screen  career stretches all the way back to the  early 1970s  as such he's been a mainstay of british  tv for decades including a brief feature  on doctor who in 2010 alongside his  house of the dragon co-star matt smith
 

